     *  OPEN or PENDING claims; none means none. Not dated. */
    @Column(name = "max_open")
    private Integer maxOpen;

    /** The proof kinds, comma separated: a claim above the proof threshold needs at least one proof of each
     *  before it can be settled or approved; none means none. Not dated. */
    @Column(name = "proof_kinds")
    private String proofKinds;

    /** The default grade: the grade a person added by the quick-add bar, or by an import line with a blank
     *  grade, takes; none means A. Not dated. */
    @Column(name = "default_grade")
    private String defaultGrade;

    /** The retired grades, comma separated in the order retired: none can be chosen for a new person or in
     *  an edit from then on, though the people on one keep it; none means none. Not dated. */
    @Column(name = "retired_grades")
    private String retiredGrades;

    /** The grades added to the sheet on top of A, B and C, comma separated in the order added; none means
     *  none. Not dated. */
    @Column(name = "added_grades")
    private String addedGrades;

    /** The month (1 to 12) a fiscal year starts in; a fiscal year is named by the calendar year its first
     *  day falls in. Not dated. */
    @Column(name = "fiscal_start_month", nullable = false)
    private int fiscalStartMonth = 1;

    /** The entry date: while set, the default date of a new claim in place of the sheet's today; none means
     *  off. Not dated. */
    @Column(name = "entry_date")
    private LocalDate entryDate;

    /** The pot: shared out among the members of each balanced pool that is a member of no other pool, by their shares; none means no pot. Not
     *  dated. */
    @Column(name = "pot", precision = 15, scale = 2)
    private BigDecimal pot;

    /** The alert threshold: a change records an ALERT for each person whose due-total goes from at or below it
     *  (or none) to above it; none means off. Not dated. */
    @Column(name = "alert_threshold", precision = 15, scale = 2)
    private BigDecimal alertThreshold;

    /** The parent sheet's id: a grade with no rate in force on a date here takes the parent's, then its
     *  parent's, up to three levels up; none means no parent. Not dated. */
    @Column(name = "parent")
    private String parent;

    /** The id of the sheet this one was cloned from: a grade with no rate in force on a date here nor on its
     *  parents takes the source's, and so on up the source's parents and source; none means not a clone. */
    @Column(name = "source")
    private String source;

    /** Whether the sheet is archived: everything stays visible and every change is refused. */
    @Column(name = "archived", nullable = false)
    private boolean archived;

    protected Sheet() {
    }

    public Sheet(String id, String createdBy, Instant createdAt, LocalDate today) {
        this.id = id;
        this.createdBy = createdBy;
        this.createdAt = createdAt;
        this.today = today;
    }

    public String getId() {
        return id;
    }

    public String getCreatedBy() {
        return createdBy;
    }

    public Instant getCreatedAt() {
        return createdAt;
    }

    public LocalDate getToday() {
        return today;
    }

    public void setToday(LocalDate today) {
        this.today = today;
    }

    /** Every value recorded for a setting that carries a figure, by key, then from-date. */
    public List<SheetSetting> getSettings() {
        return settings.stream()
                .sorted(Comparator.comparing(SheetSetting::getKey).thenComparing(SheetSetting::getFromDate))
                .toList();
    }

    /** Record a setting's value from a date, keeping its other values; one already from that date is
     *  replaced. None is a value too (no limit, no cap, a grade using the sheet's terms). */
    public void setSetting(String key, LocalDate from, String value) {
        settings.removeIf(s -> s.getKey().equals(key) && s.getFromDate().equals(from));
        settings.add(new SheetSetting(key, from, value));
    }

    /** The value of a setting in force on a date: the one with the latest from-date on or before it; empty
     *  when none is recorded by then, null inside when the one in force is none. */
    private Optional<SheetSetting> inForce(String key, LocalDate date) {
        return settings.stream()
                .filter(s -> s.getKey().equals(key) && !s.getFromDate().isAfter(date))
                .max(Comparator.comparing(SheetSetting::getFromDate));
    }

    private BigDecimal decimalOn(String key, LocalDate date, BigDecimal start) {
        return inForce(key, date).map(s -> s.getValue() == null ? null : new BigDecimal(s.getValue())).orElse(start);
    }

    /** The largest due a clerk may settle, in force on the sheet's today; none when there is no limit. */
    public BigDecimal getClerkLimit() {
        return decimalOn(CLERK_LIMIT, today, null);
    }

    /** The clerk limit for a grade, in force on the sheet's today: the grade's own (clerk-limit-<grade>) when
     *  one is set then, else the sheet's; none when neither is. */
    public BigDecimal clerkLimitFor(String grade) {
        BigDecimal own = grade == null ? null : decimalOn(CLERK_LIMIT + "-" + grade, today, null);
        return own != null ? own : getClerkLimit();
    }

    /** The least a claim's live due can be on a date; 1.00 before every from-date. */
    public BigDecimal floorOn(LocalDate date) {
        return decimalOn(FLOOR, date, START_FLOOR);
    }

    /** The floor in force on the sheet's today. */
    public BigDecimal getFloor() {
        return floorOn(today);
    }

    /** The most a person's due-total can be, in force on the sheet's today; none when there is no cap. */
    public BigDecimal getCap() {
        return decimalOn(CAP, today, null);
    }

    /** The proof threshold in force on a date: a claim dated then whose due is above it needs a proof to be
     *  settled or approved; none when there is no threshold. */
    public BigDecimal proofThresholdOn(LocalDate date) {
        return decimalOn(PROOF_THRESHOLD, date, null);
    }

    /** A grade's own proof threshold on a date; none when it has none then (and for no grade). */
    public BigDecimal gradeProofThresholdOn(String grade, LocalDate date) {
        return grade == null ? null : decimalOn(PROOF_THRESHOLD + "-" + grade, date, null);
    }

    /** The proof threshold of a grade on a date: its own when one is set then, else the sheet's. */
    public BigDecimal proofThresholdFor(String grade, LocalDate date) {
        BigDecimal own = gradeProofThresholdOn(grade, date);
        return own != null ? own : proofThresholdOn(date);
    }

    /** The proof threshold in force on the sheet's today; none when there is no threshold. */
    public BigDecimal getProofThreshold() {
        return proofThresholdOn(today);
    }

    /** The note threshold in force on a date: a claim dated then whose due is above it cannot be opened with
     *  an empty note; none when there is no threshold. */
    public BigDecimal noteThresholdOn(LocalDate date) {
        return decimalOn(NOTE_THRESHOLD, date, null);
    }

    /** The note threshold in force on the sheet's today; none when there is no threshold. */
    public BigDecimal getNoteThreshold() {
        return noteThresholdOn(today);
    }

    /** The review threshold in force on a date: a claim dated then whose due is above it goes to REVIEW when
     *  opened, for a steward to review; none when there is no threshold. */
    public BigDecimal reviewThresholdOn(LocalDate date) {
        return decimalOn(REVIEW_THRESHOLD, date, null);
    }

    /** The review threshold in force on the sheet's today; none when there is no threshold. */
    public BigDecimal getReviewThreshold() {
        return reviewThresholdOn(today);
    }

    /** A person's due-total as it counts, with their cut total: at most the cap less the cut total (not below
     *  0.00); none (n/a) stays none. */
    public BigDecimal capped(BigDecimal dueTotal, BigDecimal cutTotal) {
        BigDecimal limit = capLess(cutTotal);
        return dueTotal == null || limit == null ? dueTotal : dueTotal.min(limit);
    }

    /** The most a person's due-total can be with their cut total: the cap less it, not below 0.00; none when
     *  there is no cap. */
    public BigDecimal capLess(BigDecimal cutTotal) {
        BigDecimal cap = getCap();
        return cap == null ? null : cap.subtract(cutTotal == null ? BigDecimal.ZERO : cutTotal).max(BigDecimal.ZERO.setScale(2));
    }

    /** The sheet's terms on a date; 14 before every from-date. */
    public int termsOn(LocalDate date) {
        return inForce(TERMS, date).map(s -> Integer.valueOf(s.getValue())).orElse(START_TERMS);
    }

    /** The sheet's terms in force on its today. */
    public int getTerms() {
        return termsOn(today);
    }

    /** A grade's own terms on a date; none when it uses the sheet's terms then. */
    public Integer gradeTermsOn(String grade, LocalDate date) {
        return inForce(TERMS + "-" + grade, date).map(SheetSetting::getValue).map(Integer::valueOf).orElse(null);
    }

    /** The grades with their own terms in force on the sheet's today, and their terms. */
    public Map<String, Integer> getGradeTerms() {
        Map<String, Integer> out = new TreeMap<>();
        settings.stream().map(SheetSetting::getKey).filter(k -> k.startsWith(TERMS + "-")).distinct()
                .forEach(k -> {
                    String grade = k.substring(TERMS.length() + 1);
                    Integer own = gradeTermsOn(grade, today);
                    if (own != null) {
                        out.put(grade, own);
                    }
                });
        return out;
    }

    /** The terms of a grade on a date: its own, else the sheet's (the sheet's for no grade). */
    public int termsFor(String grade, LocalDate date) {
        Integer own = grade == null ? null : gradeTermsOn(grade, date);
        return own != null ? own : termsOn(date);
    }

    /** A grade's grace days on a date; none when it has none then (and for no grade). */
    public Integer gradeGraceOn(String grade, LocalDate date) {
        return grade == null ? null
                : inForce(GRACE + "-" + grade, date).map(SheetSetting::getValue).map(Integer::valueOf).orElse(null);
    }

    /** The date a claim's lateness runs from: its due-by plus the grace days in force on its date of its
     *  person's grade in force then (none: the due-by). It is overdue once this is before the sheet's today,
     *  and its late charge's 30-day boundaries count from it. */
    public LocalDate lateFrom(LocalDate dueBy, String grade, LocalDate date) {
        Integer grace = gradeGraceOn(grade, date);
        return grace == null ? dueBy : dueBy.plusDays(grace);
    }

    /** The late percent on a date; 0.00 before every from-date. */
    public BigDecimal latePctOn(LocalDate date) {
        return decimalOn(LATE_PCT, date, START_LATE_PCT);
    }

    /** The late percent in force on the sheet's today. */
    public BigDecimal getLatePct() {
        return latePctOn(today);
    }

    /** The roles typed for each action in the permission matrix; an action not here keeps the standing rule. */
    public Map<String, String> getPermissions() {
        return new TreeMap<>(permissions);
    }

    /** Set the roles that may take an action, comma separated; blank keeps the standing rule. */
    public void setPermission(String action, String roles) {
        if (roles == null || roles.isBlank()) {
            permissions.remove(action);
        } else {
            permissions.put(action, roles);
        }
    }

    /** Whether a role may take an action: by the permission matrix, else by the standing rule. */
    public boolean allows(String action, String role) {
        String typed = permissions.get(action);
        List<String> allowed = typed == null ? STANDING_PERMISSIONS.getOrDefault(action, List.of())
                : Arrays.stream(typed.split(",")).map(String::trim).toList();
        return allowed.contains(role);
    }

    public boolean isArchived() {
        return archived;
    }

    public void archive() {
        this.archived = true;
    }

    public LocalDate getPolicyDate() {
        return policyDate;
    }

    public void setPolicyDate(LocalDate policyDate) {
        this.policyDate = policyDate;
    }

    public LocalDate getPeriodNumberingFrom() {
        return periodNumberingFrom;
    }

    public void setPeriodNumberingFrom(LocalDate periodNumberingFrom) {
        this.periodNumberingFrom = periodNumberingFrom;
    }

    public LocalDate getEntryDate() {
        return entryDate;
    }

    public void setEntryDate(LocalDate entryDate) {
        this.entryDate = entryDate;
    }

    public BigDecimal getPot() {
        return pot;
    }

    public void setPot(BigDecimal pot) {
        this.pot = pot;
    }

    public BigDecimal getAlertThreshold() {
        return alertThreshold;
    }

    public void setAlertThreshold(BigDecimal alertThreshold) {
        this.alertThreshold = alertThreshold;
    }

    public String getParent() {
        return parent;
    }

    public void setParent(String parent) {
        this.parent = parent;
    }

    public String getSource() {
        return source;
    }

    public void setSource(String source) {
        this.source = source;
    }

    public Integer getGraceDays() {
        return graceDays;
    }

    public void setGraceDays(Integer graceDays) {
        this.graceDays = graceDays;
    }

    public Integer getEscalateAfter() {
        return escalateAfter;
    }

    public void setEscalateAfter(Integer escalateAfter) {
        this.escalateAfter = escalateAfter;
    }

    public Integer getScoreMid() {
        return scoreMid;
    }

    public void setScoreMid(Integer scoreMid) {
        this.scoreMid = scoreMid;
    }

    public Integer getScoreHigh() {
        return scoreHigh;
    }

    public void setScoreHigh(Integer scoreHigh) {
        this.scoreHigh = scoreHigh;
    }

    public boolean isScoreLog() {
        return scoreLog;
    }

    public void setScoreLog(boolean scoreLog) {
        this.scoreLog = scoreLog;
    }

    public Integer getReviewSla() {
        return reviewSla;
    }

    public void setReviewSla(Integer reviewSla) {
        this.reviewSla = reviewSla;
    }

    public Integer getPendingSla() {
        return pendingSla;
    }

    public void setPendingSla(Integer pendingSla) {
        this.pendingSla = pendingSla;
    }

    public Integer getMaxOpen() {
        return maxOpen;
    }

    public void setMaxOpen(Integer maxOpen) {
        this.maxOpen = maxOpen;
    }

    public String getProofKinds() {
        return proofKinds;
    }

    public void setProofKinds(String proofKinds) {
        this.proofKinds = proofKinds;
    }

    public String getDefaultGrade() {
        return defaultGrade;
    }

    /** The grade a new person takes when none is given: the default grade, or A when none is set or the
     *  default grade is retired. */
    public String defaultGradeOrA() {
        return defaultGrade == null || isGradeRetired(defaultGrade) ? "A" : defaultGrade;
    }

    /** The sheet's grades: A, B and C, then those added, in the order added. */
    public List<String> getGrades() {
        List<String> grades = new ArrayList<>(List.of("A", "B", "C"));
        if (addedGrades != null) {
            grades.addAll(Arrays.asList(addedGrades.split(",")));
        }
        return grades;
    }

    public boolean isGrade(String grade) {
        return getGrades().contains(grade);
    }

    /** Add a grade not yet a grade. */
    public void addGrade(String grade) {
        addedGrades = addedGrades == null ? grade : addedGrades + "," + grade;
    }

    /** The retired grades, in the order retired. */
    public List<String> getRetiredGrades() {
        return retiredGrades == null ? List.of() : Arrays.asList(retiredGrades.split(","));
    }

    public boolean isGradeRetired(String grade) {
        return getRetiredGrades().contains(grade);
    }

    /** Retire a grade not yet retired. */
    public void retireGrade(String grade) {
        retiredGrades = retiredGrades == null ? grade : retiredGrades + "," + grade;
    }

    public void setDefaultGrade(String defaultGrade) {
        this.defaultGrade = defaultGrade;
    }

    public int getFiscalStartMonth() {
        return fiscalStartMonth;
    }

    public void setFiscalStartMonth(int fiscalStartMonth) {
        this.fiscalStartMonth = fiscalStartMonth;
    }

    /** Whether a claim opened now is numbered within its period: the setting is a date and today is on or
     *  after it. */
    public boolean numbersByPeriod() {
        return periodNumberingFrom != null && !today.isBefore(periodNumberingFrom);
    }

    /** The rounding mode (half-up or half-even) in force on a date; none when none is set then. */
    public String roundingModeOn(LocalDate date) {
        return inForce(ROUNDING, date).map(SheetSetting::getValue).orElse(null);
    }

    /** The rounding mode in force on the sheet's today; none when none is set. */
    public String getRoundingMode() {
        return roundingModeOn(today);
    }

    /** How a claim dated on a date rounds its figures: by the rounding mode in force on that date; with none,
     *  half up before the policy date (the sheet's today when it has none), half to even on or after it. */
    public RoundingMode rounding(LocalDate date) {
        String mode = roundingModeOn(date);
        if (mode != null && ROUNDING_MODES.containsKey(mode)) {
            return ROUNDING_MODES.get(mode);
        }
        LocalDate policy = policyDate == null ? today : policyDate;
        return date.isBefore(policy) ? RoundingMode.HALF_UP : RoundingMode.HALF_EVEN;
    }

    /** The late charge on an overdue claim's figure: for each full 30 days past the date its lateness runs
     *  from (its due-by plus any grace, see lateFrom) on the sheet's today, the late percent in force on that
     *  boundary date (that date plus 30, 60, 90 ... days) of the
     *  figure plus the charges of the boundaries before it (compounding), rounded to cents as its date
     *  rounds, the charges added up (a boundary at 0.00 adds nothing);
     *  0.00 for no figure (n/a). Only an OPEN or PENDING claim is overdue, so the caller asks only for those. */
    public BigDecimal lateCharge(BigDecimal figure, LocalDate lateFrom, LocalDate date) {
        BigDecimal charge = BigDecimal.ZERO.setScale(2);
        if (figure == null) {
            return charge;
        }
        long boundaries = ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(lateFrom, today) / 30;
        RoundingMode rounding = rounding(date);
        for (long k = 1; k <= boundaries; k++) {
            charge = charge.add(figure.add(charge).multiply(latePctOn(lateFrom.plusDays(30 * k))).movePointLeft(2)
                    .setScale(2, rounding));
        }
        return charge;
    }

    /** A live due of a claim dated on a date as it counts: at least the floor in force then; none (n/a)
     *  stays none. */
    public BigDecimal floored(BigDecimal due, LocalDate date) {
        return due == null ? null : due.max(floorOn(date));
    }

    /** The fiscal year a date falls in, named by the calendar year its first day falls in. */
    public int fiscalYearOf(LocalDate date) {
        return date.getMonthValue() >= fiscalStartMonth ? date.getYear() : date.getYear() - 1;
    }

    public int getLastSettleBatch() {
        return lastSettleBatch;
    }

    /** Give out the sheet's next settle batch number. */
    public int nextSettleBatch() {
        return ++lastSettleBatch;
    }
}

